From ee695ffff4a02007ac983dd35ed4859c17ffefb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreyKatzburg <64795827+CoreyKatzburg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:34:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] Add rtx.drawLog.tag: one-frame per-draw scene log
 (measurement only)

For the white tanks at con_boiler: when rtx.drawLog.tag changes to a new
non-empty value, the next frame's draws that reach processDrawCallState are
written to gate\<tag>_remix_draws.tsv with geometry, material and stage-0
image hashes, the texcoord source (decl, vscapture, texgen, none), whether
the albedo was tracked for the draw and for its instance's surface material,
and whether a running USD capture holds the material and the mesh's material.
This tells the no-texcoords branch apart from the material-hash and capture
binding branches, which the proxy draw dump cannot.

Off by default. With the tag empty the only cost is one bool test per draw
(1.1 ns per draw offline) and one string test per frame; no behaviour changes.
Format and tests: rtx_draw_log.h, tools/remix tests/remix_source/draw_log_test.cpp
and tests/analysis/remix_draw_log.py.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a1e070-32c4-730c-bdfc-76d09e1f79eb
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
